% Vignette 3 — cross-border acquisition triggering CFIUS review.
%
% $1.8B acquisition of a US semiconductor design company by a foreign
% strategic acquirer based in a US-allied jurisdiction. CFIUS
% mandatory filing applies (critical technology). Low HHI overlap
% in addressable market — no HSR Second Request expected. All-cash
% deal with committed financing. Broad MAC carveouts. RTF of 5%.
% No activist position.
%
% Expected behaviour: posterior between Jane Doe friendly (vignette
% 1) and healthcare merger (vignette 2). CFIUS suppresses but other
% factors support. The user's question: "do I admit a deal to my
% pipeline at these odds?" — kickback at 50% threshold likely fires
% because CFIUS outcome is the load-bearing uncertainty.

observe regulatory(cfius_jurisdiction)
observe regulatory(no_antitrust_concern)
observe deal_structure(all_cash)
observe financing(committed_debt_no_market_out)
observe mac_clause(broad_industry_carveouts)
observe rtf_present_above_3pct

% CFIUS outcome is the load-bearing uncertainty. Three plausible
% paths: clear at notice (most favorable), 45-day investigation
% with mitigation (moderate delay), or blocked/withdrawn (worst).
% Encoded as an uncertainty over the three regulatory-status atoms
% that fire on this conclusion.
uncertain { regulatory(no_antitrust_concern),
            regulatory(regulated_industry_target),
            regulatory(hsr_second_request_likely) } for deal_completes_by_drop_dead
  source "CFIUS mitigation negotiations ongoing; outcome will resolve which regulatory atom describes the path"
  trust authoritative

? deal_completes_by_drop_dead
